WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.435
-Guys it is time for
"Tonight Show" hashtags.

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.970
Here we go.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:08.274
♪ -Hashtags ♪

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:12.412
♪ Hashtags ♪

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:15.014
-We do this thing every week
where I send out a hashtag

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:17.283
and ask you guys to respond to
that topic.

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:20.887
So, this week I sent out the
#IGotBusted and I asked you guys

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:23.289
to tweet out a story
about a time you got caught

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.425
doing something
funny or embarrassing.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:26.826
Tariq, do you get
ever caught doing something

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.728
funny or embarrassing?
-Absolutely.

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:31.731
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.800
-Within minutes,
it was a trending topic,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.902
so thank you all so much
for playing along.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.871
And now I thought I'd
share some of my favorite

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:40.006
#IGotBusted responses
from you guys.

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:43.343
This first one is
from @Brown2606.

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:45.645
She says, "When I was a
teenager, I tried to sneak out

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:46.946
of the house late one night.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:49.215
On my way out I accidentally
rang the doorbell."

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:51.250
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.853
"Honey, someone's here.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:56.055
It's our daughter."

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:58.858
This one's from @ummjello.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.493
She says,
"My sisters threw a rager

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:01.761
while my parents were away.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.196
We got rid of
all the evidence.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:05.965
The next day our parents came
home, didn't suspect a thing

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.766
until they turned on
the ceiling fan

00:01:07.766 --> 00:01:09.569
and beer bottle caps flew off."

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:12.005
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:14.374
"The fan's drinking again."

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:17.710
This one is from @joedeprospero.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.078
Wow. That's a good name.

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:21.614
He says, "I got caught playing
air guitar by myself

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.750
and tried to pretend I was
brushing lint off my shirt."

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.985
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.653
-Yeah, that always happens.

00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:30.523 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:34.126
Jimmy!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.126 --> 00:01:36.963
-This one's from @bellowssue.

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:39.632
She says, "I was riding with
a friend to her parents' house,

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.667
and we were talking about
how hideously some of the houses

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:42.935
were painted
in the neighborhood.

00:01:42.935 --> 00:01:44.270
I said,
'Whoa, look at that one.'

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:45.371
She said, 'We're here.'"

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.707
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:50.042
"That's not what -- I like it.
It's actually --

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:51.744
What is it,
like a scurvy green?"

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:53.412
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.412 --> 00:01:56.749
This one's from @christie0106.

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:59.786
She says, "When I was 16 I snuck
out to a club in Nashville.

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:01.587
My mom called the club.

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:03.389
They stopped the music
and called my name

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:06.326
across the intercom,
saying my mom was on the phone."

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:08.694
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.694 --> 00:02:11.931
That's good right there.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:16.435
This one's from
@pastorkeester -- kester.

00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:21.040
[ Laughter ]
@Pastorkester76.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:25.211
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.747
This is -- Sorry. There's one E.

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.716
@Pastorkester76.

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:30.817
-Okay.

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:34.787
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:37.857
-He says...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.325
..."I was explaining to
a co-worker

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:40.960
that I'm bad
at remembering names.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.728
'What about Adam Bell,' he asks?

00:02:42.728 --> 00:02:44.597
'Do you know
the name Adam Bell?'

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:45.598
I thought about it and said,

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.233
'It kind of sounds familiar,
but no.'

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:49.135
He replied, 'I'm Adam Bell.'"

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:51.637
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:53.006
[ Cymbal crashes ]

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:59.478
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.478 --> 00:03:00.713
Is that your favorite one?

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:02.982
-Yeah, that's pretty good.
That's pretty good.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:04.550
-Adam Bell is pretty good.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:07.687
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.355
Oh, my gosh.

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:11.323
I don't know
why it's making me laugh.

00:03:11.323 --> 00:03:12.492
Adam Bell.

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:14.359
-Like, for some reason I hear --
-"I'm Adam Bell."

00:03:14.359 --> 00:03:18.331
-I hear him saying it in, like,
the Batman voice though.

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:20.466
-[ Deep voice ] I'm Adam Bell.
-Yeah, yeah!

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:22.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:23.669
-[ Normal voice ]
But does he say the other lines

00:03:23.669 --> 00:03:24.770
like Batman, too?

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:26.205
[ Deep voice ]
"What about Adam Bell?"

00:03:26.205 --> 00:03:27.373
-Yeah, exactly.

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:28.808
-"Do you know
the name Adam Bell?

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:30.109
-[ Deep voice ] I'm Adam Bell.

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:31.878
-I'm Adam Bell.

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:33.046
-[ Normal voice ] Yeah.

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:34.514
-[ High-pitched voice ]
No, I'm Adam Bell.

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:37.317
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:39.452
-[ Deep voice ]
"I'll fight you for it."

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:43.255
-[ Normal voice ] "Will the real
Adam Bell please sta--

00:03:43.255 --> 00:03:47.026
In fact, I, the announcer,
am the real Adam Bell."

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:49.462
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:52.732
This one is from
@martinamelcherm.

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:55.401
She says, "I was in a group
interview for a sales position

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:57.170
at the Disney Store
when I burped

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.637
a cloud of marijuana smoke.

00:03:58.637 --> 00:04:01.107
It was kind of amazing,
but I didn't get the job."

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:05.011
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:08.314
It was kind of amazing?

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:09.982
-Okay.

00:04:09.982 --> 00:04:13.386
-"It was kind of amazing,
but I didn't get the job."

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:14.520
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.456
You thought that was
going to be like --

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:19.025
-I mean, you know how hard it is
to burp weed smoke?

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:21.260
[ Laughter ]
-No, I don't. I have no idea.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:22.761
-Give credit
where credit is due.

00:04:22.761 --> 00:04:24.297
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:30.002
This last one is from -- I'm not
kidding -- it's @iamjennymcd.

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:31.804
Do you know Jenny McD?

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:33.606
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:36.542
"Sounds familiar,
but, no, I don't know Je--"

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.344
I am Jenny McD.

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.179
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:41.781
Hi. I'm Adam Bell.

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:43.015
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:47.619
Want to get married?

00:04:47.619 --> 00:04:49.889
Jenny McD.

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:51.490
She says,
"On the way to a wedding,

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:52.992
an erratic driver
was ticking me off.

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:54.626
I flipped him off
as he passed us.

00:04:54.626 --> 00:04:55.795
Turns out he was the minister."

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.496
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.496 --> 00:04:58.898
Pastor Kester.

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:00.399
There you have it, everybody.

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.001
Those are "Tonight Show"
hashtags.

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:03.302
To check out
more of our favorites,

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:05.538 line:0%
go to tonightshow.com/hashtags.

